meta {
  name: Login Rate Limited (429)
  type: http
  seq: 14
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
  body: json
  auth: none
}

body:json {
  {
    "email": "{{testEmail}}",
    "password": "definitely-the-wrong-password"
  }
}

docs {
  Send this six times in a row. The first five return 401; the sixth returns
  429 with {"error": "Too many attempts", "retryAfterSeconds": N} and a
  Retry-After header.

  The limit is 5 attempts per 15 minutes per email address, plus a looser 20
  per 15 minutes per IP. The per-email bucket is the one doing the real work,
  because x-forwarded-for can be spoofed.

  Reset between runs with:

    DELETE FROM auth_rate_limits;

  The counters are in Postgres rather than process memory because Railway may
  run more than one instance, where an in-memory limiter silently becomes
  instances x limit and resets on every deploy.
}
